6. THE SELECTION (rounds 1 to 4; SUPERSEDED for F01 / D-17 by P0-1's correction (c), section 8)
   F01 / D-17 on C-ALLTX rev 3: A1, the PA held to its 30 W service by a VGG loop on board D (SESSION, within authority: no requirement,
     money or claim changes; the kit's VHF stage is a 30 W stage). It is the only approach that closes the case with the printed gauge
     bound; A2 and A3 close only the nominal deficit. Its acceptance: the loop's half-tolerance at most 0.5 dB over temperature (the case
     with the printed bounds), at most 0.25 dB to cover the 8 W modules and D-11's basis as well. CONDITIONAL on the bench row of section 4
     (the drain current at the loop's high end at VDD 13.8 V) and on a detector whose sheet prints that accuracy; not drafted: no detector
     part is held and the loop is not designed (the next deliverable: a held detector's sheet and board D's draft)
   I-03 / C-DEV: (b), the supervisors on their own buck; L9P-F04: with A1 at +-0.5 dB or tighter
   FOR C-PROT (record l9stk's, reported, not changed here): the gauge's uncalibrated one-sided error (U1, 0.8036 A) exceeds the 0.32 A between
     the 18 A service and the breaker's least limit 18.32 A (l9stk 15.4), so an under-reading gauge lets the true current reach the
     breaker's least limit while it indicates under 18 A; calibrated (U1, 0.1736 A) the error is under that gap
   OPEN: F01 / D-17 and I-03 until a draft composes and its acceptance holds on its case, and the collaborator's targeted check (V3);
     U5 (R-214), the PA bench row, the case row's quoted figure (a revision is the coordinator's)

